# 2. Preserve the most important architecture boundary

The LLM must **not** generate a final AI-6A ChangeSet.

It must not be trusted to generate:

* `before` values
* workspace revision
* before/after signatures
* stable IDs for newly inserted shots
* complete reorder arrays
* ChangeSet IDs
* Workspace IDs
* canonical state assumptions

The Director should express only:

> what creative change it wants to make.

Then deterministic backend code must convert that intent into the existing AI-6A ChangeOperation types.

The architecture must remain:

```text
LLM creative intention
        ↓
validate semantic intention
        ↓
read real Workspace project
        ↓
deterministic compiler
        ↓
existing ChangeOperation
        ↓
existing preview_changeset(...)
```

Never:

```text
LLM
↓
invented ChangeSet JSON
↓
Apply
```

